{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schema\": \"aos-material-review/v1\", \"request_id\": \"qyh-customer-lifecycle-bounded-reader-20261015-code-r1\", \"task_id\": \"qyh-customer-lifecycle-bounded-reader-20261015\", \"owner\": \"codex-01a13484-f019-7d82-94ce-812396db9124\", \"kind\": \"quality\", \"baseline\": {\"head\": \"7385617635ab7331483ad6e891e8bf5e089839e5\", \"authority_revision\": \"AOS-002036\", \"files\": {\".evidence/qyh-customer-lifecycle-bounded-reader-20261015/code-review-material-r1.txt\": \"17bb9195bacb9b569661955c24277fbb72ba087ad5688a59668efe3d770499cd\"}}, \"claims\": [\"客户reader在同一核实只读RR快照中读取四完整保存修订COUNT及有界latest Batch/exact ancestor/policies，SQL尺寸与时间门、outer metadata与稳定错误防止失败伪装空成功。\", \"选中保存事实按原policy请求签名、typed refs/typed ledger与item hashes、prepare/freeze完整继承及lineage核验；strict raw/tenant/time/隐私和零效果保留unknown，不产生Contact或当前Consent准入。\", \"冻结仅四owned overlay的387专项及相邻测试、原w6_007临时PG真快照/RLS/25006/SQLCASE/metadata拒绝物证与已停止CID支持此候选；未部署、不宣称真实经营或完整Goal完成。\"], \"materials\": {\".evidence/qyh-customer-lifecycle-bounded-reader-20261015/code-review-material-r1.txt\": \"READER CODE QUALITY ONLY, NOT DEPLOYED. Full231Goal ACTIVE. Original domain writer/Store/DDL unchanged. Independent design PASS legally consumed. Synthetic native PG uses only disposable tmpfs, not original business DB or real Consent authority.\\n\\nFULL FILE services/aos-api/aos_api/ecommerce_customer_lifecycle_readonly.py SHA b7ac470efd1d04f36621896d830b094562fb899ab223fb73555f03bc88617010\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Read saved customer revisions without contact resolution or operational admission.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nfrom time import monotonic\\n\\nimport psycopg\\nfrom psycopg import IsolationLevel\\n\\nfrom aos_api.db import connect_read_only\\nfrom aos_api import ecommerce_workshop_customer_lifecycle as domain\\nfrom aos_api.public_contracts import redact_sensitive\\n\\nMAX_ROW_BYTES = 1024 * 1024\\nMAX_TOTAL_BYTES = 8 * MAX_ROW_BYTES\\nBATCH_TABLE = 'ecommerce_customer_dialogue_batch_revision'\\nPOLICIES = (\\n    ('ecommerce_customer_consent_policy_revision', 'policy_id', domain.CustomerConsentPolicyRevision, domain.CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest, 'consent_policy'),\\n    ('ecommerce_customer_segment_revision', 'segment_id', domain.CustomerSegmentRevision, domain.CreateCustomerSegmentRequest, 'segment'),\\n    ('ecommerce_customer_journey_revision', 'journey_id', domain.CustomerJourneyRevision, domain.CreateCustomerJourneyRequest, 'journey'),\\n    ('ecommerce_customer_dialogue_strategy_revision', 'dialogue_id', domain.CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision, domain.CreateCustomerDialogueRequest, 'dialogue'),\\n)\\n_FREEZE_EXCLUDE = {'revision', 'version', 'lifecycle', 'prior_content_hash', 'content_hash', 'created_by', 'created_at'}\\n_INTS = {'revision', 'version', 'retentionDays', 'kAnonymityMinimum', 'input', 'eligible', 'excluded',\\n         'needsReview', 'unknown', 'deduplicated', 'contactResolutionCount', 'actionCount',\\n         'providerCallCount', 'sendCount', 'externalEffectCount'}\\n_BOOLS = {'originalsReachable', 'retentionActive', 'kAnonymitySatisfied'}\\n_NULLABLE_BOOLS = {'retentionActive', 'kAnonymitySatisfied'}\\n_REFS = {'segment': 'segment_ref', 'journey': 'journey_ref', 'dialogue': 'dialogue_ref',\\n         'consentPolicy': 'consent_policy_ref', 'frequencyPolicy': 'frequency_policy_ref',\\n         'channelCapability': 'channel_capability_ref'}\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError(RuntimeError):\\n    def __init__(self, code):\\n        self.code = code\\n        super().__init__(code)\\n\\n\\ndef _deny(suffix):\\n    raise CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError('CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_READ_' + suffix)\\n\\n\\ndef _aware(value):\\n    return isinstance(value, datetime) and value.utcoffset() is not None\\n\\n\\ndef _strict(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\n        for key, child in value.items():\\n            if key in _INTS and type(child) is not int: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n            if key in _BOOLS and type(child) is not bool and not (key in _NULLABLE_BOOLS and child is None):\\n                _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n            _strict(child)\\n    elif isinstance(value, list):\\n        for child in value: _strict(child)\\n\\n\\ndef _visible(value):\\n    # Hash syntax and full producer hashes are checked separately; avoid matching\\n    # accidental digit sequences inside hashes as if they were phone numbers.\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\n        return {k: _visible(v) for k, v in value.items() if not k.endswith(('Hash', 'Hashes'))}\\n    if isinstance(value, list): return [_visible(v) for v in value]\\n    return value\\n\\n\\ndef _privacy(raw):\\n    visible = _visible(raw)\\n    if redact_sensitive(visible) != visible: _deny('SENSITIVE_CONTENT')\\n    serialized = json.dumps(visible, ensure_ascii=False).lower()\\n    if any(word in serialized for word in ('mobile', 'openid', 'email', 'address', 'nickname', 'avatar', 'rawmessage', 'providerpayload')):\\n        _deny('SENSITIVE_CONTENT')\\n\\n\\ndef _request(model, item):\\n    return model.model_validate({name: getattr(item, name) for name in model.model_fields})\\n\\n\\ndef _matches(ref, item, identity):\\n    return (ref.resource_id == getattr(item, identity) and ref.revision == item.revision\\n            and ref.content_hash == 'sha256:' + item.content_hash)\\n\\n\\nclass _ValidatedStore:\\n    def __init__(self, counts, batch): self.counts, self.batch = counts, batch\\n    def authority_counts(self, _scope): return self.counts\\n    def latest_batch_or_none_any(self, _scope): return self.batch\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerLifecycleReadonlyReader:\\n    def __init__(self, *, connect_factory=None):\\n        self._connect = connect_factory or connect_read_only\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _count(conn, scope, table, identity):\\n        # Identifiers are fixed POLICIES constants, never request input. These\\n        # are counts of ALL stored revisions, not distinct or active customers.\\n        alias = ''.join(part.title() if index else part for index, part in enumerate(identity.split('_')))\\n        valid = (f\\\"length({identity}) BETWEEN 1 AND 200 AND revision>=1 \\\"\\n                 f\\\"AND content_hash ~ '^[0-9a-f]{{64}}$' \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND jsonb_typeof(authority_data)='object' \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND authority_data->'tenant'->'orgId'=to_jsonb(org_id) \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND authority_data->'tenant'->'projectId'=to_jsonb(project_id) \\\"\\n                 f\\\"AND authority_data->'{alias}'=to_jsonb({identity}) \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND authority_data->'revision'=to_jsonb(revision) \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND authority_data->'contentHash'=to_jsonb(content_hash::text) \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND jsonb_typeof(authority_data->'createdAt')='string' \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND authority_data->>'createdAt' ~ '(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$' \\\"\\n                 \\\"AND (authority_data->>'createdAt')::timestamptz=created_at\\\")\\n        return conn.execute(f'SELECT COUNT(*) AS count, '\\n                            f'SUM(CASE WHEN {valid} THEN 0 ELSE 1 END) AS invalid_count, '\\n                            f'MAX(created_at) AS latest_created_at FROM {table} '\\n                            'WHERE org_id=%s AND project_id=%s', scope.key).fetchone()\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _row(conn, scope, table, identity, exact=None):\\n        # At most one payload per query, bounded in SQL before transfer.\\n        sql = (f'SELECT org_id,project_id,CASE WHEN length({identity})<=200 THEN {identity} ELSE NULL END AS identity,'\\n               'revision,CASE WHEN length(content_hash)=64 THEN content_hash ELSE NULL END AS content_hash,'\\n               'created_at,octet_length(authority_data::text) AS size,'\\n               f'CASE WHEN octet_length(authority_data::text)<={MAX_ROW_BYTES} THEN authority_data ELSE NULL END AS authority_data '\\n               f'FROM {table} WHERE org_id=%s AND project_id=%s ')\\n        params = scope.key\\n        if exact is not None:\\n            sql += f'AND {identity}=%s AND revision=%s '\\n            params = (*params, *exact)\\n        return conn.execute(sql + f'ORDER BY created_at DESC,revision DESC,{identity} LIMIT 1', params).fetchone()\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _decode(row, model, identity, scope, cutoff):\\n        if row is None: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if ((row.get('org_id'), row.get('project_id')) != scope.key\\n                or not isinstance(row.get('identity'), str) or not 0 < len(row['identity']) <= 200\\n                or type(row.get('revision')) is not int or row['revision'] < 1\\n                or not isinstance(row.get('content_hash'), str) or re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', row['content_hash']) is None\\n                or not _aware(row.get('created_at')) or row['created_at'] > cutoff): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if type(row.get('size')) is not int or row['size'] < 1: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if row['size'] > MAX_ROW_BYTES: _deny('LIMIT_EXCEEDED')\\n        raw = row.get('authority_data')\\n        if not isinstance(raw, dict): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        _strict(raw)\\n        item = model.model_validate(raw)\\n        if item.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True) != raw: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if ((item.tenant.org_id, item.tenant.project_id) != scope.key or getattr(item, identity) != row['identity']\\n                or item.revision != row['revision'] or item.content_hash != row['content_hash']\\n                or not _aware(item.created_at) or item.created_at != row['created_at']\\n                or item.created_at > cutoff): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if hasattr(item, 'cutoff') and (not _aware(item.cutoff) or item.cutoff > cutoff): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        _privacy(raw)\\n        return item\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _validate_batch(item, prior=None):\\n        request = _request(domain.PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchRequest, item)\\n        refs = {key: getattr(request, attr) for key, attr in _REFS.items()}\\n        hashes = [domain.canonical_hash(value.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True)) for value in request.items]\\n        counts = {kind: sum(value.disposition == kind for value in request.items) for kind in domain.CustomerBatchDisposition}\\n        ledger = domain.CustomerDialogueBatchLedger(input=len(request.items), **{key.value: value for key, value in counts.items()})\\n        binding = domain.canonical_hash({'refs': refs, 'itemHashes': hashes})\\n        if item.item_hashes != hashes or item.binding_hash != binding or item.ledger != ledger: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if any(getattr(item, field) != 0 for field in ('contact_resolution_count', 'action_count', 'provider_call_count', 'send_count', 'external_effect_count')):\\n            _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        if item.lifecycle == 'prepared':\\n            expected = domain.canonical_hash({**request.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True), 'ledger': ledger, 'bindingHash': binding})\\n            if item.revision != 1 or item.version != 1 or item.prior_content_hash is not None or item.content_hash != expected:\\n                _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        elif item.lifecycle == 'frozen':\\n            if prior is None or prior.lifecycle != 'prepared': _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n            CustomerLifecycleReadonlyReader._validate_batch(prior)\\n            if (item.revision != prior.revision + 1 or item.version != prior.version + 1\\n                    or item.prior_content_hash != prior.content_hash or item.created_at < prior.created_at): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n            inherited = prior.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True, exclude=_FREEZE_EXCLUDE)\\n            if item.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True, exclude=_FREEZE_EXCLUDE) != inherited: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n            expected = domain.canonical_hash({**inherited, 'revision': item.revision, 'version': item.version,\\n                                              'lifecycle': 'frozen', 'priorContentHash': prior.content_hash})\\n            if item.content_hash != expected: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n        else: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n\\n    def read(self, scope):\\n        started = monotonic()\\n        def deadline():\\n            if monotonic() - started > 10: _deny('LIMIT_EXCEEDED')\\n        try:\\n            with self._connect(scope) as conn:\\n                if conn.read_only is not True or conn.autocommit is not False or conn.isolation_level != IsolationLevel.REPEATABLE_READ:\\n                    _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                conn.execute(\\\"SET LOCAL statement_timeout='3000ms'\\\")\\n                conn.execute(\\\"SET LOCAL lock_timeout='500ms'\\\")\\n                cutoff = conn.execute('SELECT transaction_timestamp() AS cutoff').fetchone()['cutoff']\\n                if not _aware(cutoff): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                counts = {}\\n                for table, identity, _model, _request_model, key in POLICIES:\\n                    deadline()\\n                    aggregate = self._count(conn, scope, table, identity)\\n                    count, invalid, latest = (aggregate[k] for k in ('count', 'invalid_count', 'latest_created_at'))\\n                    if type(count) is not int or not 0 <= count <= 2**53 - 1: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                    # SUM over no rows is SQL NULL; all other aggregates must be strict integers.\\n                    if not ((count == 0 and invalid is None) or (type(invalid) is int and invalid == 0)): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                    if count == 0 and latest is not None: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                    if count and (not _aware(latest) or latest > cutoff): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                    counts[key] = count\\n                deadline()\\n                selected = self._row(conn, scope, BATCH_TABLE, 'batch_id')\\n                batch = None\\n                if selected is not None:\\n                    total = 0\\n                    def decode(row, model, identity):\\n                        nonlocal total\\n                        item = self._decode(row, model, identity, scope, cutoff)\\n                        total += row['size']\\n                        if total > MAX_TOTAL_BYTES: _deny('LIMIT_EXCEEDED')\\n                        return item\\n                    batch = decode(selected, domain.CustomerDialogueBatchRevision, 'batch_id')\\n                    prior = None\\n                    if batch.lifecycle == 'frozen':\\n                        deadline()\\n                        prior = decode(self._row(conn, scope, BATCH_TABLE, 'batch_id', (batch.batch_id, batch.revision - 1)),\\n                                       domain.CustomerDialogueBatchRevision, 'batch_id')\\n                    self._validate_batch(batch, prior)\\n                    facts = {}\\n                    for table, identity, model, request_model, key in POLICIES:\\n                        deadline()\\n                        if counts[key] < 1: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                        ref = getattr(batch, key + '_ref')\\n                        fact = decode(self._row(conn, scope, table, identity, (ref.resource_id, ref.revision)), model, identity)\\n                        if not _matches(ref, fact, identity): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                        request = _request(request_model, fact)\\n                        if fact.content_hash != domain.canonical_hash(request.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True)): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                        facts[key] = fact\\n                    if (facts['segment'].consent_policy_ref != batch.consent_policy_ref\\n                            or facts['journey'].segment_ref != batch.segment_ref\\n                            or facts['dialogue'].journey_ref != batch.journey_ref\\n                            or facts['dialogue'].eval_ref != facts['journey'].eval_ref): _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                deadline()\\n                view = domain.EcommerceWorkshopCustomerLifecycleService(_ValidatedStore(counts, batch)).contribution_view(scope, now=cutoff)\\n                payload = view.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True)\\n                payload['allowedCommands'] = []\\n                result = domain.CustomerLifecycleContributionView.model_validate(payload)\\n                if result.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True) != payload: _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n                if len(result.model_dump_json(by_alias=True).encode()) > MAX_ROW_BYTES: _deny('LIMIT_EXCEEDED')\\n                deadline()\\n                return result\\n        except CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError:\\n            raise\\n        except psycopg.Error:\\n            _deny('AUTHORITY_UNAVAILABLE')\\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, KeyError, AttributeError, OverflowError):\\n            _deny('AUTHORITY_DRIFT')\\n\\n\\nFULL FILE services/aos-api/tests/test_ecommerce_customer_lifecycle_readonly.py SHA 7a987406dcf9def751b096f5a2e3cf53d1d2698da8cad3402a047195abda8f2f\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Saved customer facts, not contact/consent admission; synthetic producer fixtures.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom datetime import timedelta\\nimport importlib.util\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport psycopg\\nfrom psycopg import IsolationLevel\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom aos_api import ecommerce_customer_lifecycle_readonly as reader\\n\\n\\ndef producer_fixture(frozen=True):\\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('customer_read_fixture', Path(__file__).parent / 'aip/test_w6_07_customer_lifecycle.py')\\n    f = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(f)\\n    f.SCOPE = f.TenantScope('dev-org', 'fixture-project')\\n    def exact(item, kind, identity):\\n        name = getattr(item, identity)\\n        return f.CustomerExactRef(resourceType=kind, resourceId=name, revision=item.revision,\\n                                 contentHash='sha256:' + item.content_hash, receiptId='receipt-' + name)\\n    f.exact = exact\\n    store, service, *refs = f.authority_fixture()\\n    batch = service.prepare_batch(f.SCOPE, f.batch_request(*refs), 'synthetic-operator', now=f.NOW)\\n    if frozen:\\n        names = {'segment': 'segment_ref', 'journey': 'journey_ref', 'dialogue': 'dialogue_ref',\\n                 'consentPolicy': 'consent_policy_ref', 'frequencyPolicy': 'frequency_policy_ref', 'channelCapability': 'channel_capability_ref'}\\n        service.freeze_batch(f.SCOPE, batch.batch_id, f.FreezeCustomerDialogueBatchRequest(\\n            expectedVersion=1, expectedContentHash=batch.content_hash,\\n            exactRefs={k: getattr(batch, v) for k, v in names.items()}, itemHashes=batch.item_hashes),\\n            'synthetic-reviewer', now=f.NOW + timedelta(seconds=1))\\n    data = {}\\n    for table, identity, _model, _request, name in reader.POLICIES:\\n        attr = {'consent_policy': 'policies', 'segment': 'segments', 'journey': 'journeys', 'dialogue': 'dialogues'}[name]\\n        data[table] = [row(item, identity) for item in getattr(store, attr).values()]\\n    data[reader.BATCH_TABLE] = [row(item, 'batch_id') for item in store.batches[batch.batch_id]]\\n    return f, data\\n\\n\\ndef row(item, identity):\\n    raw = item.model_dump(mode='json', by_alias=True)\\n    return dict(org_id=item.tenant.org_id, project_id=item.tenant.project_id,\\n                identity=getattr(item, identity), revision=item.revision, content_hash=item.content_hash,\\n                created_at=item.created_at, size=len(json.dumps(raw).encode()), authority_data=raw)\\n\\n\\nclass Result:\\n    def __init__(self, value): self.value = value\\n    def fetchone(self): return self.value\\n\\n\\nclass Connection:\\n    read_only = True\\n    autocommit = False\\n    isolation_level = IsolationLevel.REPEATABLE_READ\\n    def __init__(self, data, cutoff):\\n        self.data, self.cutoff, self.calls, self.overrides = deepcopy(data), cutoff, [], {}\\n    def __enter__(self): return self\\n    def __exit__(self, *args): pass\\n    def execute(self, sql, params=None):\\n        self.calls.append((sql, params))\\n        if sql.startswith('SET LOCAL'): return Result(None)\\n        if 'transaction_timestamp()' in sql: return Result({'cutoff': self.cutoff})\\n        table = next(t for t in self.data if 'FROM ' + t + ' ' in sql)\\n        rows = self.data[table]\\n        if 'COUNT(*)' in sql:\\n            assert params == ('dev-org', 'fixture-project') and 'LIMIT' not in sql\\n            return Result(self.overrides.get(table, dict(count=len(rows), invalid_count=0,\\n                          latest_created_at=max((r['created_at'] for r in rows), default=None))))\\n        assert 'LIMIT 1' in sql and 'CASE WHEN octet_length' in sql\\n        assert params[:2] == ('dev-org', 'fixture-project')\\n        if len(params) > 2: rows = [r for r in rows if (r['identity'], r['revision']) == tuple(params[2:])]\\n        return Result(deepcopy(max(rows, key=lambda r: (r['created_at'], r['revision'], r['identity']))) if rows else None)\\n\\n\\ndef run(data=None, frozen=True):\\n    f, original = producer_fixture(frozen)\\n    conn = Connection(original if data is None else data, f.NOW + timedelta(seconds=2))\\n    return f, conn, reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyReader(connect_factory=lambda scope: conn)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('frozen', [False, True])\\ndef test_original_typed_producer_hashes_and_unknown_remain(frozen):\\n    f, conn, subject = run(frozen=frozen)\\n    view = subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n    assert view.tenant.org_id == 'dev-org' and view.primary_colleague == '私域管家'\\n    assert view.consent_policy_count == view.segment_count == view.journey_count == view.dialogue_count == 1\\n    assert view.latest_batch.lifecycle == ('frozen' if frozen else 'prepared')\\n    assert view.latest_batch.ledger.eligible == view.latest_batch.ledger.unknown == 1\\n    unknown = view.latest_batch.items[1]\\n    assert unknown.consent_decision.value == 'unknown' and unknown.retention_active is unknown.k_anonymity_satisfied is None\\n    assert view.allowed_commands == []\\n    assert not any((view.contact_resolution_allowed, view.start_allowed, view.send_allowed, view.external_effects_allowed))\\n    assert len([s for s, _ in conn.calls if 'COUNT(*)' in s]) == 4\\n\\n\\ndef test_real_empty_and_complete_saved_revision_count():\\n    f, conn, subject = run()\\n    for table in conn.data: conn.data[table] = []\\n    conn.overrides[reader.POLICIES[0][0]] = dict(count=9000, invalid_count=0, latest_created_at=f.NOW)\\n    view = subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n    assert view.consent_policy_count == 9000 and view.segment_count == 0 and view.latest_batch is None\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('field,value', [('count', True), ('count', -1), ('count', 2**53), ('invalid_count', 1), ('invalid_count', False)])\\ndef test_invalid_aggregate_is_never_empty_success(field, value):\\n    f, conn, subject = run()\\n    entry = dict(count=1, invalid_count=0, latest_created_at=f.NOW); entry[field] = value\\n    conn.overrides[reader.POLICIES[0][0]] = entry\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('attribute,value', [('read_only', False), ('autocommit', True), ('isolation_level', IsolationLevel.READ_COMMITTED)])\\ndef test_snapshot_contract_required(attribute, value):\\n    f, conn, subject = run(); setattr(conn, attribute, value)\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('mutation', ['tenant', 'hash', 'itemHash', 'bindingHash', 'prior', 'inherited', 'unknown', 'bool', 'missing', 'extra', 'privacy', 'oversize', 'time', 'stale', 'policyHash', 'lineage'])\\ndef test_saved_tampering_rejected(mutation):\\n    f, conn, subject = run(); latest = conn.data[reader.BATCH_TABLE][-1]; raw = latest['authority_data']\\n    if mutation == 'tenant': raw['tenant']['orgId'] = 'foreign'\\n    elif mutation == 'hash': raw['contentHash'] = 'a' * 64\\n    elif mutation == 'itemHash': raw['itemHashes'][0] = 'b' * 64\\n    elif mutation == 'bindingHash': raw['bindingHash'] = 'c' * 64\\n    elif mutation == 'prior': raw['priorContentHash'] = 'd' * 64\\n    elif mutation == 'inherited': raw['items'][0]['itemKey'] = 'changed'\\n    elif mutation == 'unknown': raw['items'][1]['disposition'] = 'eligible'\\n    elif mutation == 'bool': raw['sendCount'] = False\\n    elif mutation == 'missing': del raw['actionCount']\\n    elif mutation == 'extra': raw['mobile'] = 'fixture-private-value'\\n    elif mutation == 'privacy': raw['createdBy'] = 'fixture@example.test'\\n    elif mutation == 'oversize': latest['size'] = reader.MAX_ROW_BYTES + 1; latest['authority_data'] = None\\n    elif mutation == 'time': latest['created_at'] = conn.cutoff + timedelta(seconds=1)\\n    elif mutation == 'stale': raw['lifecycle'] = 'stale'\\n    elif mutation == 'policyHash': conn.data[reader.POLICIES[0][0]][0]['authority_data']['purpose'] = 'changed'\\n    elif mutation == 'lineage': conn.data[reader.POLICIES[1][0]][0]['authority_data']['consentPolicyRef']['resourceId'] = 'different'\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\ndef test_future_aggregate_not_hidden_by_cutoff_filter():\\n    f, conn, subject = run()\\n    conn.overrides[reader.POLICIES[0][0]] = dict(count=1, invalid_count=0, latest_created_at=conn.cutoff + timedelta(seconds=1))\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\ndef test_database_failure_is_stable_not_fake_zero():\\n    f, conn, subject = run()\\n    def fail(*args): raise psycopg.OperationalError('private database details')\\n    conn.execute = fail\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError, match='CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_READ_AUTHORITY_UNAVAILABLE'): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\ndef test_time_budget_checked_between_queries(monkeypatch):\\n    f, conn, subject = run(); ticks = iter([0, 11])\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(reader, 'monotonic', lambda: next(ticks))\\n    with pytest.raises(reader.CustomerLifecycleReadonlyError, match='LIMIT_EXCEEDED'): subject.read(f.SCOPE)\\n\\n\\nFULL FILE services/aos-api/aos_api/ecommerce_workshop_customer_lifecycle.py SHA 0c1cb897d99b622d041d65688bedceedd5697da1fdd6152844fcd0e2bfa3ac4d\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"W6-07 customer lifecycle authority and side-effect-free batch preparation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\\nfrom enum import StrEnum\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\nfrom pydantic import Field, field_validator, model_validator\\n\\nfrom aos_api.aip_contracts import AipContractModel, TenantContext\\nfrom aos_api.ecommerce_workshop_customer_contracts import CustomerExactRef\\nfrom aos_api.tenant_scope import TenantScope\\n\\n\\nCUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_SCHEMA_VERSION = \\\"aos.ecommerce-workshop.customer-lifecycle/v1\\\"\\nCUSTOMER_LOGIC_ID = \\\"ecommerce-customer-relationship\\\"\\nCUSTOMER_SKILL_IDS = (\\n    \\\"build-evidence-pack\\\",\\n    \\\"segment-entities\\\",\\n    \\\"consent-and-purpose-check\\\",\\n    \\\"needs-discovery\\\",\\n    \\\"customer-journey-plan\\\",\\n    \\\"response-or-outreach-draft\\\",\\n    \\\"verify-claims\\\",\\n    \\\"review-outcomes\\\",\\n)\\n\\n\\ndef canonical_hash(value: Any) -> str:\\n    payload = json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\"), default=str)\\n    return hashlib.sha256(payload.encode()).hexdigest()\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerLifecycleBlocked(RuntimeError):\\n    code = \\\"CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_BLOCKED\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerLifecycleConflict(CustomerLifecycleBlocked):\\n    code = \\\"CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_CONFLICT\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass ConsentDecision(StrEnum):\\n    GRANTED = \\\"granted\\\"\\n    WITHDRAWN = \\\"withdrawn\\\"\\n    EXPIRED = \\\"expired\\\"\\n    UNKNOWN = \\\"unknown\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerBatchDisposition(StrEnum):\\n    ELIGIBLE = \\\"eligible\\\"\\n    EXCLUDED = \\\"excluded\\\"\\n    NEEDS_REVIEW = \\\"needs_review\\\"\\n    UNKNOWN = \\\"unknown\\\"\\n    DEDUPLICATED = \\\"deduplicated\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _unique(values: list[str], label: str) -> list[str]:\\n    if len(values) != len(set(values)) or any(not value.strip() for value in values):\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"{label} must be unique and non-empty\\\")\\n    return values\\n\\n\\ndef _unique_refs(values: list[CustomerExactRef], label: str) -> list[CustomerExactRef]:\\n    identities = [(ref.resource_type, ref.resource_id, ref.revision, ref.content_hash, ref.receipt_id) for ref in values]\\n    if len(identities) != len(set(identities)):\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"{label} must be unique\\\")\\n    return values\\n\\n\\nclass CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    policy_id: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    revision: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    purpose: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=160)\\n    allowed_channels: list[str] = Field(min_length=1, max_length=16)\\n    marking_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    retention_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    preference_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    retention_days: int = Field(ge=1, le=3650)\\n    unknown_behavior: str = Field(default=\\\"block\\\", pattern=r\\\"^block$\\\")\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _canonical(self) -> \\\"CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest\\\":\\n        _unique(self.allowed_channels, \\\"allowedChannels\\\")\\n        expected = (\\n            (self.marking_policy_ref, \\\"MarkingPolicyRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.retention_policy_ref, \\\"RetentionPolicyRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.preference_policy_ref, \\\"PreferencePolicyRevision\\\"),\\n        )\\n        if any(ref.resource_type != kind for ref, kind in expected):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"customer consent policy exact refs drifted\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerConsentPolicyRevision(CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest):\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    created_by: str\\n    created_at: datetime\\n\\n\\nclass CreateCustomerSegmentRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    segment_id: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    revision: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    definition_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    query_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    schema_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    source_refs: list[CustomerExactRef] = Field(min_length=1, max_length=100)\\n    consent_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    k_anonymity_minimum: int = Field(ge=5, le=10000)\\n    cutoff: datetime\\n\\n    @field_validator(\\\"cutoff\\\")\\n    @classmethod\\n    def _aware(cls, value: datetime) -> datetime:\\n        if value.utcoffset() is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"cutoff must include timezone\\\")\\n        return value\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _refs(self) -> \\\"CreateCustomerSegmentRequest\\\":\\n        if self.schema_ref.resource_type != \\\"SegmentSchemaRevision\\\" or self.consent_policy_ref.resource_type != \\\"CustomerConsentPolicyRevision\\\":\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"segment schema or consent policy ref drifted\\\")\\n        if any(ref.resource_type not in {\\\"CustomerLiteProjectionRevision\\\", \\\"SourceReadinessRevision\\\"} for ref in self.source_refs):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"segment source refs must remain privacy-minimized\\\")\\n        _unique_refs(self.source_refs, \\\"sourceRefs\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerSegmentRevision(CreateCustomerSegmentRequest):\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    created_by: str\\n    created_at: datetime\\n\\n\\nclass CreateCustomerJourneyRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    journey_id: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    revision: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    segment_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    stage_definition_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    entry_condition_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    exit_condition_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    stop_conditions: list[str] = Field(min_length=1, max_length=32)\\n    allowed_channels: list[str] = Field(min_length=1, max_length=16)\\n    eval_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _refs(self) -> \\\"CreateCustomerJourneyRequest\\\":\\n        expected = ((self.segment_ref, \\\"CustomerSegmentRevision\\\"), (self.eval_ref, \\\"EvalContractRevision\\\"), (self.policy_ref, \\\"JourneyPolicyRevision\\\"))\\n        if any(ref.resource_type != kind for ref, kind in expected):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"journey exact refs drifted\\\")\\n        _unique(self.stop_conditions, \\\"stopConditions\\\")\\n        _unique(self.allowed_channels, \\\"allowedChannels\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerJourneyRevision(CreateCustomerJourneyRequest):\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    created_by: str\\n    created_at: datetime\\n\\n\\nclass CreateCustomerDialogueRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    dialogue_id: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    revision: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    journey_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    brief_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    evidence_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    eval_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    responsibility_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    template_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    strategy_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    originals_reachable: bool\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _refs(self) -> \\\"CreateCustomerDialogueRequest\\\":\\n        expected = (\\n            (self.journey_ref, \\\"CustomerJourneyRevision\\\"), (self.brief_ref, \\\"TaskBriefRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.evidence_ref, \\\"EvidenceBundleRevision\\\"), (self.eval_ref, \\\"EvalContractRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.responsibility_ref, \\\"ResponsibilityPlanRevision\\\"), (self.template_ref, \\\"TemplateRevision\\\"),\\n        )\\n        if any(ref.resource_type != kind for ref, kind in expected):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"dialogue exact refs drifted\\\")\\n        if not self.originals_reachable:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"dialogue originals must remain reachable\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision(CreateCustomerDialogueRequest):\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    created_by: str\\n    created_at: datetime\\n\\n\\nclass PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchItem(AipContractModel):\\n    item_key: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    customer_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    disposition: CustomerBatchDisposition\\n    consent_decision: ConsentDecision\\n    retention_active: bool | None\\n    k_anonymity_satisfied: bool | None\\n    reason_codes: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list, max_length=32)\\n    eligibility_evidence_refs: list[CustomerExactRef] = Field(default_factory=list, max_length=32)\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _privacy_and_disposition(self) -> \\\"PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchItem\\\":\\n        if self.customer_ref.resource_type != \\\"CustomerLiteProjectionRevision\\\":\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"batch item only accepts CustomerLiteProjectionRevision\\\")\\n        _unique(self.reason_codes, \\\"reasonCodes\\\")\\n        _unique_refs(self.eligibility_evidence_refs, \\\"eligibilityEvidenceRefs\\\")\\n        eligible = self.consent_decision is ConsentDecision.GRANTED and self.retention_active is True and self.k_anonymity_satisfied is True and bool(self.eligibility_evidence_refs)\\n        if self.disposition is CustomerBatchDisposition.ELIGIBLE and (not eligible or self.reason_codes):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"eligible item requires exact granted consent/retention/k-anonymity evidence\\\")\\n        if self.disposition is not CustomerBatchDisposition.ELIGIBLE and not self.reason_codes:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"non-eligible item requires reasonCodes\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerDialogueBatchLedger(AipContractModel):\\n    input: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    eligible: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    excluded: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    needs_review: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    unknown: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    deduplicated: int = Field(ge=0)\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _conserves(self) -> \\\"CustomerDialogueBatchLedger\\\":\\n        if self.input != self.eligible + self.excluded + self.needs_review + self.unknown + self.deduplicated:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"customer batch ledger must conserve input\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    batch_id: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=200)\\n    segment_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    journey_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    dialogue_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    consent_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    frequency_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    channel_capability_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    items: list[PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchItem] = Field(min_length=1, max_length=1000)\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def _refs(self) -> \\\"PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchRequest\\\":\\n        expected = (\\n            (self.segment_ref, \\\"CustomerSegmentRevision\\\"), (self.journey_ref, \\\"CustomerJourneyRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.dialogue_ref, \\\"CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision\\\"), (self.consent_policy_ref, \\\"CustomerConsentPolicyRevision\\\"),\\n            (self.frequency_policy_ref, \\\"FrequencyPolicyRevision\\\"), (self.channel_capability_ref, \\\"CapabilityBindingRevision\\\"),\\n        )\\n        if any(ref.resource_type != kind for ref, kind in expected):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"customer batch exact refs drifted\\\")\\n        _unique([item.item_key for item in self.items], \\\"itemKeys\\\")\\n        return self\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerDialogueBatchRevision(AipContractModel):\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    batch_id: str\\n    revision: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    version: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    lifecycle: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^(prepared|frozen|stale)$\\\")\\n    segment_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    journey_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    dialogue_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    consent_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    frequency_policy_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    channel_capability_ref: CustomerExactRef\\n    items: list[PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchItem]\\n    item_hashes: list[str]\\n    ledger: CustomerDialogueBatchLedger\\n    binding_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    contact_resolution_count: int = Field(default=0, ge=0, le=0)\\n    action_count: int = Field(default=0, ge=0, le=0)\\n    provider_call_count: int = Field(default=0, ge=0, le=0)\\n    send_count: int = Field(default=0, ge=0, le=0)\\n    external_effect_count: int = Field(default=0, ge=0, le=0)\\n    prior_content_hash: str | None = Field(default=None, pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    created_by: str\\n    created_at: datetime\\n\\n\\nclass FreezeCustomerDialogueBatchRequest(AipContractModel):\\n    expected_version: int = Field(ge=1)\\n    expected_content_hash: str = Field(pattern=r\\\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\\\")\\n    exact_refs: dict[str, CustomerExactRef]\\n    item_hashes: list[str]\\n\\n\\nclass CustomerLifecycleContributionView(AipContractModel):\\n    schema_version: str = CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_SCHEMA_VERSION\\n    tenant: TenantContext\\n    evaluated_at: datetime\\n    atomic_skill_ids: list[str] = Field(default_factory=lambda: list(CUSTOMER_SKILL_IDS))\\n    logic_id: str = CUSTOMER_LOGIC_ID\\n    primary_colleague: str = \\\"私域管家\\\"\\n    collaborator_colleagues: list[str] = Field(default_factory=lambda: [\\\"内容官\\\", \\\"客服专员\\\", \\\"导购顾问\\\", \\\"数据参谋\\\"])\\n    consent_policy_count: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    segment_count: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    journey_count: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    dialogue_count: int = Field(ge=0)\\n    latest_batch: CustomerDialogueBatchRevision | None\\n    blockers: list[str]\\n    allowed_commands: list[str] = Field(default_factory=lambda: [\\n        \\\"CREATE_CUSTOMER_CONSENT_POLICY\\\", \\\"CREATE_CUSTOMER_SEGMENT\\\", \\\"CREATE_CUSTOMER_JOURNEY\\\",\\n        \\\"CREATE_CUSTOMER_DIALOGUE\\\", \\\"PREPARE_CUSTOMER_DIALOGUE_BATCH\\\", \\\"FREEZE_CUSTOMER_DIALOGUE_BATCH\\\",\\n    ])\\n    contact_resolution_allowed: bool = False\\n    start_allowed: bool = False\\n    send_allowed: bool = False\\n    external_effects_allowed: bool = False\\n\\n\\nclass EcommerceWorkshopCustomerLifecycleService:\\n    def __init__(self, store: Any) -> None:\\n        self.store = store\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _tenant(scope: TenantScope) -> TenantContext:\\n        return TenantContext(org_id=scope.org_id, project_id=scope.project_id)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _ref(resource_type: str, resource_id: str, revision: int, content_hash: str) -> CustomerExactRef:\\n        return CustomerExactRef(resourceType=resource_type, resourceId=resource_id, revision=revision, contentHash=f\\\"sha256:{content_hash}\\\", receiptId=f\\\"receipt-{resource_id}\\\")\\n\\n    def _create(self, scope: TenantScope, request: Any, actor: str, model: type[Any], append: Any, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> Any:\\n        at = now or datetime.now(UTC)\\n        payload = request.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\", by_alias=True)\\n        item = model(tenant=self._tenant(scope), **payload, contentHash=canonical_hash(payload), createdBy=actor, createdAt=at)\\n        return append(scope, item)\\n\\n    def create_consent_policy(self, scope: TenantScope, request: CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerConsentPolicyRevision:\\n        return self._create(scope, request, actor, CustomerConsentPolicyRevision, self.store.append_consent_policy, now=now)\\n\\n    def create_segment(self, scope: TenantScope, request: CreateCustomerSegmentRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerSegmentRevision:\\n        self.store.require_consent_policy(scope, request.consent_policy_ref)\\n        return self._create(scope, request, actor, CustomerSegmentRevision, self.store.append_segment, now=now)\\n\\n    def create_journey(self, scope: TenantScope, request: CreateCustomerJourneyRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerJourneyRevision:\\n        self.store.require_segment(scope, request.segment_ref)\\n        return self._create(scope, request, actor, CustomerJourneyRevision, self.store.append_journey, now=now)\\n\\n    def create_dialogue(self, scope: TenantScope, request: CreateCustomerDialogueRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision:\\n        journey = self.store.require_journey(scope, request.journey_ref)\\n        if journey.eval_ref != request.eval_ref:\\n            raise CustomerLifecycleBlocked(\\\"CUSTOMER_DIALOGUE_JOURNEY_EVAL_DRIFTED\\\")\\n        return self._create(scope, request, actor, CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision, self.store.append_dialogue, now=now)\\n\\n    def prepare_batch(self, scope: TenantScope, request: PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerDialogueBatchRevision:\\n        at = now or datetime.now(UTC)\\n        segment = self.store.require_segment(scope, request.segment_ref)\\n        journey = self.store.require_journey(scope, request.journey_ref)\\n        dialogue = self.store.require_dialogue(scope, request.dialogue_ref)\\n        self.store.require_consent_policy(scope, request.consent_policy_ref)\\n        if journey.segment_ref != request.segment_ref or dialogue.journey_ref != request.journey_ref or segment.consent_policy_ref != request.consent_policy_ref:\\n            raise CustomerLifecycleBlocked(\\\"CUSTOMER_BATCH_LINEAGE_DRIFTED\\\")\\n        self.store.require_external_policy_authorities(scope, request.frequency_policy_ref, request.channel_capability_ref)\\n        counts = {item: 0 for item in CustomerBatchDisposition}\\n        for item in request.items:\\n            counts[item.disposition] += 1\\n        ledger = CustomerDialogueBatchLedger(\\n            input=len(request.items), eligible=counts[CustomerBatchDisposition.ELIGIBLE],\\n            excluded=counts[CustomerBatchDisposition.EXCLUDED], needsReview=counts[CustomerBatchDisposition.NEEDS_REVIEW],\\n            unknown=counts[CustomerBatchDisposition.UNKNOWN], deduplicated=counts[CustomerBatchDisposition.DEDUPLICATED],\\n        )\\n        refs = {\\n            \\\"segment\\\": request.segment_ref, \\\"journey\\\": request.journey_ref, \\\"dialogue\\\": request.dialogue_ref,\\n            \\\"consentPolicy\\\": request.consent_policy_ref, \\\"frequencyPolicy\\\": request.frequency_policy_ref,\\n            \\\"channelCapability\\\": request.channel_capability_ref,\\n        }\\n        item_hashes = [canonical_hash(item.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\", by_alias=True)) for item in request.items]\\n        binding_hash = canonical_hash({\\\"refs\\\": refs, \\\"itemHashes\\\": item_hashes})\\n        payload = request.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\", by_alias=True)\\n        content_hash = canonical_hash({**payload, \\\"ledger\\\": ledger, \\\"bindingHash\\\": binding_hash})\\n        existing = self.store.latest_batch_or_none(scope, request.batch_id)\\n        if existing is not None:\\n            if existing.content_hash == content_hash:\\n                return existing\\n            raise CustomerLifecycleConflict(\\\"CUSTOMER_BATCH_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT\\\")\\n        item = CustomerDialogueBatchRevision(\\n            tenant=self._tenant(scope), batchId=request.batch_id, revision=1, version=1, lifecycle=\\\"prepared\\\",\\n            segmentRef=request.segment_ref, journeyRef=request.journey_ref, dialogueRef=request.dialogue_ref,\\n            consentPolicyRef=request.consent_policy_ref, frequencyPolicyRef=request.frequency_policy_ref,\\n            channelCapabilityRef=request.channel_capability_ref, items=request.items, itemHashes=item_hashes,\\n            ledger=ledger, bindingHash=binding_hash, contentHash=content_hash, createdBy=actor, createdAt=at,\\n        )\\n        return self.store.append_batch(scope, item)\\n\\n    def freeze_batch(self, scope: TenantScope, batch_id: str, request: FreezeCustomerDialogueBatchRequest, actor: str, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerDialogueBatchRevision:\\n        at = now or datetime.now(UTC)\\n        current = self.store.latest_batch(scope, batch_id)\\n        if current.lifecycle != \\\"prepared\\\" or current.version != request.expected_version or current.content_hash != request.expected_content_hash:\\n            raise CustomerLifecycleConflict(\\\"CUSTOMER_BATCH_EXPECTED_VERSION_OR_HASH_DRIFTED\\\")\\n        expected_refs = {\\n            \\\"segment\\\": current.segment_ref, \\\"journey\\\": current.journey_ref, \\\"dialogue\\\": current.dialogue_ref,\\n            \\\"consentPolicy\\\": current.consent_policy_ref, \\\"frequencyPolicy\\\": current.frequency_policy_ref,\\n            \\\"channelCapability\\\": current.channel_capability_ref,\\n        }\\n        if request.exact_refs != expected_refs or request.item_hashes != current.item_hashes:\\n            raise CustomerLifecycleConflict(\\\"CUSTOMER_BATCH_EXACT_REFS_OR_ITEMS_DRIFTED\\\")\\n        payload = current.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\", by_alias=True, exclude={\\\"revision\\\", \\\"version\\\", \\\"lifecycle\\\", \\\"prior_content_hash\\\", \\\"content_hash\\\", \\\"created_by\\\", \\\"created_at\\\"})\\n        content_hash = canonical_hash({**payload, \\\"revision\\\": current.revision + 1, \\\"version\\\": current.version + 1, \\\"lifecycle\\\": \\\"frozen\\\", \\\"priorContentHash\\\": current.content_hash})\\n        frozen = current.model_copy(update={\\\"revision\\\": current.revision + 1, \\\"version\\\": current.version + 1, \\\"lifecycle\\\": \\\"frozen\\\", \\\"prior_content_hash\\\": current.content_hash, \\\"content_hash\\\": content_hash, \\\"created_by\\\": actor, \\\"created_at\\\": at})\\n        return self.store.append_batch(scope, frozen)\\n\\n    def contribution_view(self, scope: TenantScope, *, now: datetime | None = None) -> CustomerLifecycleContributionView:\\n        blockers: list[str] = []\\n        try:\\n            counts = self.store.authority_counts(scope)\\n            latest = self.store.latest_batch_or_none_any(scope)\\n        except CustomerLifecycleBlocked as exc:\\n            counts = {\\\"consent_policy\\\": 0, \\\"segment\\\": 0, \\\"journey\\\": 0, \\\"dialogue\\\": 0}\\n            latest = None\\n            blockers.append(str(exc))\\n        blockers.extend([\\\"CUSTOMER_CONTACT_RESOLUTION_NOT_AUTHORIZED\\\", \\\"CUSTOMER_START_SEND_NOT_AUTHORIZED\\\"])\\n        return CustomerLifecycleContributionView(\\n            tenant=self._tenant(scope), evaluatedAt=now or datetime.now(UTC),\\n            consentPolicyCount=counts[\\\"consent_policy\\\"], segmentCount=counts[\\\"segment\\\"],\\n            journeyCount=counts[\\\"journey\\\"], dialogueCount=counts[\\\"dialogue\\\"], latestBatch=latest, blockers=blockers,\\n        )\\n\\n\\n__all__ = [\\n    \\\"CUSTOMER_LIFECYCLE_SCHEMA_VERSION\\\", \\\"CUSTOMER_LOGIC_ID\\\", \\\"CUSTOMER_SKILL_IDS\\\", \\\"ConsentDecision\\\",\\n    \\\"CustomerBatchDisposition\\\", \\\"CustomerConsentPolicyRevision\\\", \\\"CustomerDialogueBatchLedger\\\",\\n    \\\"CustomerDialogueBatchRevision\\\", \\\"CustomerDialogueStrategyRevision\\\", \\\"CustomerJourneyRevision\\\",\\n    \\\"CustomerLifecycleBlocked\\\", \\\"CustomerLifecycleConflict\\\", \\\"CustomerLifecycleContributionView\\\",\\n    \\\"CustomerSegmentRevision\\\", \\\"CreateCustomerConsentPolicyRequest\\\", \\\"CreateCustomerDialogueRequest\\\",\\n    \\\"CreateCustomerJourneyRequest\\\", \\\"CreateCustomerSegmentRequest\\\", \\\"EcommerceWorkshopCustomerLifecycleService\\\",\\n    \\\"FreezeCustomerDialogueBatchRequest\\\", \\\"PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchItem\\\", \\\"PrepareCustomerDialogueBatchRequest\\\",\\n]\\n\\n\\nEVIDENCE .evidence/qyh-customer-contribution-read-admission-20261015/implementation-plan-r1.md\\n# 客户贡献保存读取：文件级实施方案\\n\\n## 基线与军规\\n\\n基线m1 7385617635ab7331483ad6e891e8bf5e089839e5、Authority2036、同owner customer-contribution-read-admission和maintenance-r9至08UTC。已复习产品v2/09、技术55-W6-07含Aug25实施封板、原models/service/Store/w6_007和前端parser。完整231Goal/原唯一真人授权/daily每次aos最新m1同原卷全面PG→API→Web/aos2不重启保留。\\n\\n只读已保存Consent policy/Segment/Journey/Dialogue修订计数和最新Batch。CustomerLite ref不是ProtectedContact，历史granted/evidence不证明当前Consent/retention/purpose或可联系；不调用prepare/freeze/create/resolver，不读商城源、不解析contact、不start/send/Provider。原生产external policy resolver恒拒绝，读取不解除它。原业务DBREADONLY/HostworkerProviderOFF/unknown旧12不重放/disabledSchedule不启用/noPush、不覆盖用户dirty。\\n\\n## 文件与登记\\n\\nparent已拥有router与read_http、本E、原D-wave。另Task先登记：\\n\\n- `services/aos-api/aos_api/ecommerce_customer_lifecycle_readonly.py`：新专用reader、原typed请求及hash验证、同snapshot完整计数/选中batch与exact ancestry、尺寸/隐私/时间/稳定错误。\\n- `services/aos-api/tests/test_ecommerce_customer_lifecycle_readonly.py`：原producer fixture、metadata/完整counts/strict raw/typed hash/lineage/未知同意/零效果/失败门。\\n\\nparent只改`services/aos-api/aos_api/routers/ecommerce_workshop.py`与`services/aos-api/tests/test_ecommerce_workshop_read_http.py`，仅canonical GET `/views/customer/contributions`用typed ReadCatalog installed-readonly分流。legacy成功及全部POST、contact/closure辅入口不改；不改原producer/Store/DDL/Web/parser/CSS/AIP或锁文件，额外文件先登记。\\n\\n## 一致截止面与完整COUNT语义\\n\\n原counts是四表全部已保存修订的COUNT(*)，不是distinct identity、活跃同意人数或逐行政策有效性背书；保留完整计数，不设截断取样后冒充总数。用一个已核实READ ONLY REPEATABLE READ连接和transaction_timestamp cutoff。固定statement_timeout3000ms/lock_timeout500ms，查询间及返回前monotonic10秒门。\\n\\n四个固定COUNT SQL仅返回count、invalid_count、latest_created_at。invalid_count检查outer id长度、payload tenant/id/revision/contentHash与外层对应及createdAt有时区且与外层时间一致；无效时间cast失败亦稳定非200。MAX created_at超过cutoff拒绝，不加WHERE时间条件隐藏未来坏行。COUNT不向客户端传输policy payload，不执行全表fetchall，也不声称重算过所有未展示policy的content hash。返回count必须原生int、0到2^53-1；任何错误整视图失败，不能补0。\\n\\n最新batch用固定表、tenant双列、ORDER created_at DESC/revision DESC/batch_id和LIMIT1，SQLCASE先限制单行1MiB/outer id200字符。frozen再读同id exact前版；selected batch的consentPolicy/segment/journey/dialogue四exact refs各取固定表一行。合计最多6payload行/8MiB，DTO1MiB，所有查询有界且同snapshot。没有batch时仍返回可信四COUNT，不读无关policy载荷。batch存在则各对应count至少1。原计数包含所有修订，例同policy rev1+rev2计2；exact旧refs仍定位旧版本，不强制最新policy。\\n\\n## 选中事实与原签名\\n\\n每payload完整字段/strict int与bool、None只在原nullable合同处、原model_dump JSON与raw一致，outer tenant/id/revision/hash/created_at与payload匹配且不晚于cutoff。selected四policy重建原Create request JSON核content hash及exact ref，核segment→consentPolicy、journey→segment、dialogue→journey/eval一致。只作保存历史lineage，不启动当前授权resolver。\\n\\nBatch用原Prepare request模型校验1000项以内、itemKeys唯一、CustomerLite类型、eligible consent/retention/k/evidence及非eligible理由，逐项重算itemHashes和五桶ledger。bindingHash按原typed refs+itemHashes，经原canonical_hash(default=str)；prepared contentHash按request JSON+typed CustomerDialogueBatchLedger对象+bindingHash，不能改用JSON ledger。prepared只能rev/version1/priorNone；frozen必须exact prepared前版、rev/version递增且所有七字段排除后的继承内容相等，再按原完整payload签名。无已识别stale writer则拒绝，不猜新签名。contactResolution/action/providerCall/send/externalEffect五counts必须原生int0。\\n\\n全部输出相关字段及selected policy通过原redact_sensitive与前端禁披露字段门，typed hash单独验证后排除其误判为电话；拒绝PII/任意扩展而非脱敏后假称原hash仍有效。不给raw message/Provider payload/成员PII披露。最终复用原contribution_view的Skill/Logic/数字同事/阻断布局，输入是已验证的纯保存适配器；完整DTO重验，commands[]及contactResolution/start/send/external四false。DB/validation/limit/privacy错误稳定503，真实空才0/null。\\n\\n## Loop与门禁\\n\\n先本E原producer纯内存probe（修正原测试approximate ref为完整exact hash），核6个typed refs、typed ledger签名、prepare/freeze继承、eligible/unknown及零效果；明确内存resolver非生产权限。独立方案Prime PASS合法消费前不改产品。\\n\\nRED含原404/异常补0风险、计数全修订/同snapshot/未来坏行、batch两生命周期/引用旧policy、raw缺字段/数字bool/隐私/unknown不造eligible、SQLCASE及稳定非200；实施后专项/原W6-07及相邻price/closure/catalog冻结累计，原w6_007隔离tmpfs PG/COUNT rev2/并发快照/RLS/25006/SQLCASE/privacy，独立reader和route质量。精确提交后fresh维护freeze/controller门/新意图API-only、原真人SDK/400/401、原650全等、客户页三视口原稿/核心只读及livePrime、准确Delivery/Authority七强/下一登记helper。\\n\\n回滚只撤该GET准入及专用reader增量，经fresh维护门，不reset或动原库。API-only不代替daily全面重启；真实Consent/预算/自然经营首链/安装全生命周期/八真实场景全视觉/观察发布仍未完成，不以页面/测试/fixture或PASS收窄完整Goal。\\n\\n\\nEVIDENCE .evidence/qyh-customer-contribution-read-admission-20261015/design-review-consumption-r1.json\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"aos-material-review-consumption/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"request_id\\\": \\\"qyh-customer-contribution-read-admission-20261015-design-r1\\\",\\n  \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"qyh-customer-contribution-read-admission-20261015\\\",\\n  \\\"owner\\\": \\\"codex-01a13484-f019-7d82-94ce-812396db9124\\\",\\n  \\\"baseline\\\": {\\n    \\\"head\\\": \\\"7385617635ab7331483ad6e891e8bf5e089839e5\\\",\\n    \\\"authority_revision\\\": \\\"AOS-002036\\\",\\n    \\\"files\\\": {\\n      \\\".evidence/qyh-customer-contribution-read-admission-20261015/design-review-material-r1.txt\\\": \\\"5c32b3bc59fc759199e62cb6f729646d8e9d057d39e19a57c7241df99d17823a\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"CONSUMED_MATERIAL_REVIEW\\\",\\n  \\\"execution_authorized\\\": false,\\n  \\\"result_sha256\\\": \\\"8f802e487af59a1993ea57fbe1a7216176cc04f43fd9d3fa70d5b44d6d6ca2cb\\\",\\n  \\\"transport_sha256\\\": \\\"c11555caa4b4c286eea9b8476fb3c91d8a1a4153fac56763b350edbad80e9139\\\"\\n}\\n\\nEVIDENCE .evidence/qyh-customer-lifecycle-bounded-reader-20261015/source-verification-r1.json\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceBefore\\\": {\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/aos_api/ecommerce_cu